# Project Context (via Horizon)

Project: ShopFlow

ShopFlow is a modern e-commerce platform using Horizon for structured 
AI context management. All project knowledge is organized through 
.purpose files, gate.yaml authorization, and the .dream overview.

This project uses Horizon for structured AI context:
- `.purpose` files define features, components, and context
- `gate.yaml` files define authorization topology
- `.dream` files aggregate everything into the Dreamscape

## How to Use Horizon

- Check .purpose files in directories before making changes
- Run `horizon status` to see all symbols in the project
- Run `horizon visualize` to explore the Dreamscape canvas
- Reference symbols using @ # $ % ~ ^ ! ? prefixes
- Look for `gate.yaml` when dealing with authorization

## Symbol System

Use these prefixes to reference project elements:

| Symbol | Name | Owner | Examples |
|--------|------|-------|----------|
| `@` | Feature | purpose | @checkout-flow, @user-login |
| `#` | Component | purpose | #ProductCard, #CartDrawer |
| `$` | Flow | shared | $checkout-to-confirmation, $auth-flow |
| `%` | State | purpose | %user.authenticated, %cart.items |
| `~` | Aspect | purpose | @login~validation, #Button~disabled |
| `^` | Gate | gate | ^auth-required, ^premium-checkout |
| `!` | Signal | gate | !payment-failed, !login-failed |
| `?` | Idea | dream | ?subscription-model, ?ai-recommendations |

### Symbol Details

- **`@` Feature** (purpose): User-facing capabilities (checkout, login, cart, etc.)
- **`#` Component** (purpose): Reusable UI components and code modules
- **`$` Flow** (shared): Multi-step user journeys and processes
- **`%` State** (purpose): Global application and user state
- **`~` Aspect** (purpose): Cross-cutting concerns and nested properties
- **`^` Gate** (gate): Access control and authorization points
- **`!` Signal** (gate): Events, errors, and side effects
- **`?` Idea** (dream): Free-form exploration and future features

## Defined States

- `%user.authenticated` - User is logged in
- `%user.role` - enum (guest, customer, admin, owner)
- `%user.subscription` - enum (free, premium, enterprise)
- `%user.emailVerified` - Email has been verified
- `%cart.items` - Items currently in cart
- `%cart.total` - Cart total in cents
- `%checkout.step` - enum (cart, shipping, payment, review, processing, complete)

## When to Update Horizon Files

- When adding a feature, create/update the nearest .purpose file
- When adding authorization logic, update gate.yaml
- When exploring new ideas, add them to .dream with ? prefix
- Always update references when renaming or moving symbols
- Run `horizon cursorrules` after updating .horizon

## Conventions

- Use kebab-case for all symbol IDs (checkout-flow, not checkoutFlow)
- Document flows when logic spans 3+ components
- Reference related items using symbol prefixes
- Add descriptions to all features, components, and gates
- Use signals for side effects (! prefix), not direct state mutations
- Keep gates minimal - one responsibility per gate
- Group related ideas in .dream under areas
- Update purpose files when changing feature behavior

## Horizon Commands

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `horizon init` | Initialize Horizon in a project |
| `horizon status` | Show project symbol status |
| `horizon visualize` | Open the Dreamscape visualizer |
| `horizon purpose validate` | Validate .purpose files |
| `horizon gate validate` | Validate gate.yaml files |
| `horizon dream aggregate` | Aggregate all symbols |
| `horizon cursorrules` | Regenerate this .cursorrules file |

## Purpose File Locations

`.purpose` files should exist in:
- `auth/` (depth: 1)
- `payments/` (depth: 1)
- `features/` (depth: 1)
- `components/` (depth: 1)

